)","Beef stock (400ml)","Tomato puree (2 tbsp)","Worcestershire sauce (2 tbsp)","Butter (30g)","Frozen peas (200g)"],"instructions":"Brown the mince, soften onion and carrot, add puree, Worcestershire and stock, simmer 30 min, stir in the peas. Top with mashed sweet potato and bake 25 min at 200C. Portion into containers before it fully cools so it firms up in shape. Reheats evenly in a microwave, unlike most baked dishes.","portions":5,"inPlan":false,"day":"Unassigned","_ings":[{"n":"Beef mince, 5% fat","q":750,"u":"g","d":"","raw":"Beef mince, 5% fat (750g)"},{"n":"Sweet potato","q":1.2,"u":"kg","d":"","raw":"Sweet potato (1.2kg)"},{"n":"Carrot","q":3,"u":"","d":"","raw":"Carrot (3)"},{"n":"Onion","q":2,"u":"","d":"","raw":"Onion (2)"},{"n":"Beef stock","q":400,"u":"ml","d":"","raw":"Beef stock (400ml)"},{"n":"Tomato puree","q":2,"u":"tbsp","d":"","raw":"Tomato puree (2 tbsp)"},{"n":"Worcestershire sauce","q":2,"u":"tbsp","d":"","raw":"Worcestershire sauce (2 tbsp)"},{"n":"Butter","q":30,"u":"g","d":"","raw":"Butter (30g)"},{"n":"Frozen peas","q":200,"u":"g","d":"","raw":"Frozen peas (200g)"}]},{"id":"p6","title":"Lentil, chickpea & spinach dhal","tag":"Meal prep","prep":true,"base":5,"macros":[450,22,66,10],"ingredients":["Red lentils (400g)","Chickpeas (2 tins)","Chopped tomatoes (1 tin)","Coconut milk (1 tin)","Onion (2)","Garlic (4 cloves)","Ginger (30g)","Curry powder (2 tbsp)","Spinach (200g)","Vegetable stock (800ml)"],"instructions":"Soften onion, garlic and ginger with the spices, add lentils, tomatoes, coconut milk and stock, simmer 30 min until the lentils collapse. Stir the spinach through at the end. Thickens in the fridge, so loosen with a splash of water when reheating. The cheapest protein on this list and it holds for the full two days.","portions":5,"inPlan":false,"day":"Unassigned","_ings":[{"n":"Red lentils","q":400,"u":"g","d":"","raw":"Red lentils (400g)"},{"n":"Chickpeas","q":2,"u":"tins","d":"","raw":"Chickpeas (2 tins)"},{"n":"Chopped toma